# CREDITS — Eighth Fold

A 40-second film in the Red Paper-cut style, made entirely in code.
The keeper, the sheet, the boat and the story are invented. No real person, brand or place is portrayed.

## Voice
Speech synthesis: Kokoro (kokoro-onnx), voice `af_heart`, English, offline.
Model and engine follow the licences of the kokoro-onnx project
(https://github.com/thewh1teagle/kokoro-onnx).

## Music
Original score, written for this film (`music/score.py`).
Pipa notes are physically modelled (`core/audio/pluck.py`).
The erhu glide is synthesised in `music/score.py` (a bowed tone with vibrato). The Karoryfer erhu samples are not in this library checkout, so none were used.
Flute stands in for a dizi. Dan tranh stands in for a zheng.

Samples (CC0 1.0):
- VS Chamber Orchestra: Community Edition (Versilian Studios) — flute
- Versilian Community Sample Library (Versilian Studios) — dan tranh, dan tranh tremolo, woodblock, frame drum, gong

## Typefaces
- Cormorant Garamond — SIL Open Font License 1.1 (Catharsis Fonts). Files copied from the Impasto demo’s `source/fonts/`, which vendors the same OFL family. See `fonts/OFL.txt`.

## Picture
Every frame is drawn by this film’s paper-cut code (`paper.js`, `film.js`).
No stock footage, no photographs, no third-party images.

## Sound effects
All foley is synthesised for this film (`mix.py`): room hush, a paper fold, crease tap, scissors, scrap drop, palm pat, unfold snaps, scrap lift, boat slide, paper peel, cardboard step, lamp swell.

